 Root Signature and Bindless
   (where RPI == Root Parameter Index)
 
 RPI        Data		Base Register

 0    		   ***		b3
 1		   ***		t0

 High level here is how you attach Resources to PSOs
 1) RPI is the sequential layout of the Root Structure Table
 2) Base Register tells you how the Shader variables will use said resources(data)

 So your task is to layout Data in Bind points and attach Base Registers to them.
 That is the purpose of Root Signatures

---  ---------- ---------- ---------- ---------- ---------- ---------- ---------- ---------- ----------
  Creating a Root Signature

  https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/direct3d12/creating-a-root-signature

  Root Signature can contain (a) inline Constants (b) inline Descriptors (c) Descriptor Ranges (pointer to Descriptor Heap)

       { RPI + Sampler } -> { ROOT_SIGNATURE_DESC } -> { RSBlob } -> { ID3D12RootSignature (use in Command List) }

       { RPI + Sampler }
     1) Start with CD3DX12_ROOT_PARAMETER1 rpi[N];

     2) Fill in individual fields with combinations of (a), (b) and (c)

     3) Use CD3DX12_STATIC_SAMPLER samplers[M] and fill them up

     	{ Root_signature_desc }
     4) CD3DX12_VERSIONED_ROOT_SIGNATURE_DESC rsDesc(TotalElements,rpi,totalSamplers,samplers);

     	{ RSBlob }
     5) D3D12SerializeVersionedRootSignature(&rsDesc, &rsBlob);

         { Root Signature }
     6)	ID3D12RootSignature* rootSignature;
        pDevice->CreateRootSignature(
	      rsBlob->GetBufferPointer(),
	      rsBlob->GetBufferSize(),
	      __uuidof(ID3D12RootSignature),
	      &rootSignature);

	 { Use in Command List }
     7) CommandList::SetGraphicsRootSignature(rootSignature);

